## Step 2B: Triage — Route to Correct Pipeline

**Before Step 3**, classify the task type. **⚠️ IMMEDIATELY persist `task-type` to harness-state.md** — this must happen BEFORE scaffold (Step 1) blocking questions can interrupt the flow.

| Signal | Task Type | harness-state.md |
|--------|-----------|------------------|
| PRD, feature spec, "design", "HLD", "LLD", new capability spanning 3+ modules, new external integrations, architectural changes, protocol changes | **Design-first** | Set `task-type: DESIGN_FIRST`, `pipeline-stage: DESIGNING` |
| HLD already exists | **HLD exists** | Set `task-type: DESIGN_FIRST`, `pipeline-stage: DESIGNING` |
| LLD already exists | **LLD exists** | Set `task-type: DESIGN_FIRST`, `pipeline-stage: PLANNING` |
| Bug fix, refactor, config change, well-scoped feature (large: 2+ files) | **Implementation (large)** | Set `task-type: IMPLEMENTATION_LARGE`, `pipeline-stage: PLANNING` |
| Bug fix, config change, single-file feature | **Implementation (small)** | Set `task-type: IMPLEMENTATION_SMALL`, `pipeline-stage: IMPLEMENTING` |

**⚠️ Do NOT proceed to scaffold without persisting `task-type`. If scaffold blocking questions interrupt the flow, harness-setup must be able to re-read `task-type` to know which agent to trigger.**

**⚠️ PRDs and new-capability tasks MUST go through designer → HLD → LLD. Skipping produces execution plans without architectural grounding.**

### Step 0C: Confluence Parent Page (Mandatory)

**⛔ Required.** Collect the Confluence parent page URL/ID. All design docs and plans are published as child pages with LGTM approval gates. Do NOT proceed without it.

`scripts/agent/confluence.sh` is guaranteed present from Checks 7–10 above.

**Dispatch `confluence-agent` with `OPERATION: SETUP_AUTH`.**
On `CONFLUENCE_AUTH_OK`: proceed. On `CONFLUENCE_AUTH_FAILED`: HARD STOP — prompt `! bash scripts/agent/confluence.sh setup`.

Persist: `confluence-review: ENABLED`, `confluence-parent-page: <id>`, `confluence-base-url: https://flipkart.atlassian.net/wiki`

### Step 0D: Jira Initiative (Mandatory)

**⛔ Required.** Collect the Jira **initiative** key/URL (not epic). The harness auto-creates an epic for this feature under the initiative via `jira-agent`, then all stories (HLD, LLD, feature splits) are created under that epic. Do NOT proceed without an initiative.

`scripts/agent/jira.sh` is guaranteed present from Checks 7–10 above.

**Dispatch `jira-agent` with `OPERATION: SETUP_AUTH`.**
On `JIRA_AUTH_OK`: proceed. On `JIRA_AUTH_FAILED`: HARD STOP — prompt `! bash scripts/agent/jira.sh setup`.

**Then dispatch `jira-agent` with `OPERATION: SETUP_EPIC`.**
It resolves the initiative key, verifies access, creates the epic (idempotent — skips if `jira-epic` already set).
On `JIRA_EPIC_CREATED:<key>:<url>`: proceed. On `JIRA_ERROR:*`: HARD STOP.

Persist: `jira-initiative: <key>`, `jira-epic: <auto-created-epic-key>`, `jira-base-url: https://flipkart.atlassian.net`. If resuming and `jira-epic` already set, `jira-agent` skips creation automatically.

### Step 0E: Repos Involved (Mandatory)

**⛔ Required.** Always ask which repos are involved — even single-repo tasks must confirm. Prevents mid-pipeline surprises. User confirms "just this repo" or provides paths to all affected repos. For multi-repo: designer produces cross-repo PRD, harness-setup spawns parallel pipelines (shared libraries first, consumers after).

Persist: `cross-repo: ENABLED|SINGLE`, `cross-repo-paths: [...]`

If secondary repos lack harness agents, offer to install them via `install.sh`.

### Step 0F: GitHub Integration (Optional)

For all task types that produce code. Ask user whether the harness should push the validated branch and open / sync a PR after every LGTM. If enabled, validate.md (after LGTM) runs `github.sh test-auth` → `push-branch` → `ensure-pr`, then persists `github-pr-number` and `github-pr-url`. Once a PR exists, the user can ask "check PR comments" and `pr-review.md` fetches reviewer feedback, asks which to implement, and routes through execute → validate → push (or back to harness-setup for SCOPE_CHANGE).

Persist: `github-integration: ENABLED|SKIP`, `github-base-url: https://github.fkinternal.com` (default; override per-repo).

If auth fails: prompt user to run `! bash scripts/agent/github.sh setup`. Setup expects a GitHub Personal Access Token (classic) with scopes `repo`, `read:org`. GHES tokens: `<github-base-url>/settings/tokens`. Credentials are stored in `.github-credentials` (gitignored, 0600).

### Step 0G: SonarQube Project (Mandatory)

**⛔ Required.** Collect the SonarQube project key or dashboard URL. Validate will not emit LGTM until Sonar coverage ≥ 90% and zero BLOCKER/CRITICAL issues. Flipkart instances: `https://service.sonar-prod.fkcloud.in` (default) or `http://service-lta.sonar-prod.fkcloud.in` (LTA).

`scripts/agent/sonar.sh` is guaranteed present from Checks 7–10 above.

Dispatch sonar-agent to resolve the project key and verify auth:
```
Dispatch sonar-agent with:
  OPERATION:  RESOLVE_PROJECT
  INPUT:      <user-provided URL or project key>
```

On `SONAR_PROJECT_RESOLVED:<key>`: agent has persisted `sonar-project-key` and `sonar-base-url` to harness-state.md. Proceed.

On `SONAR_AUTH_FAILED`: sonar-agent surfaces the setup prompt. Wait for user to run `! bash scripts/agent/sonar.sh setup`, then re-dispatch.

If resuming and `sonar-project-key` already set: dispatch sonar-agent `SETUP_AUTH` to verify credentials are still valid. Skip re-asking the user.

### Step 0H: App Runtime Mode (Ask Once Per Feature)

After SonarQube setup, ask the user how the application should run during the validate loop:

```
How should the application run during validation?

  1) Docker  — full stack in Docker Compose (default)
               `docker compose up -d` boots app + all dependencies + Vector + VictoriaLogs

  2) Local   — app runs as native process; observability stack (Vector + VictoriaLogs) in Docker
               `docker compose up -d vector victorialogs` then `bash scripts/agent/boot.sh`
               App writes structured JSON logs to stdout/stderr → Vector tails → VictoriaLogs

Enter 1 or 2:
```

**If Local mode selected:** verify that `boot.sh` can start the app natively (Python venv, Go binary, Maven exec, etc.). If `boot.sh` does not support local execution, update it or warn the user.

**Persist:** `app-runtime: docker|local`

**If already set in `harness-state.md` (resuming a session): skip this question.**

